WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.200
Your presentation just ended.

2
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:06.640
A recorded voice introduces itself
and starts asking about your project.

3
00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:09.830
«Pourquoi avez-vous choisi le
Sénégal ?» You hear it twice.

4
00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:13.010
Then a clock starts: 40 seconds.

5
00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:14.700
Then a second question.

6
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.730
A third. A fourth.

7
00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:19.170
You haven't seen any of them in advance.

8
00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:21.980
Tempted to open every answer
with «C'est une question

9
00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:24.040
intéressante» to buy time?

10
00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:26.240
Lifesaver, or trap?

11
00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:30.050
So how do you sound ready for
questions you can't predict?

12
00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:32.570
In this mission, you'll
follow the whole exchange,

13
00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:35.190
from the first hello to the fourth answer.

14
00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:39.410
Then you'll build a 40-second
answer about «l'attaya» in the lab,

15
00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:40.890
chip by chip.

16
00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:45.010
Your mission: work out how to
sound ready for all four questions.
